 "answer": "In promptfoo, the option that runs a transform on the LLM output before assertions is the `options.transform` directive. According to the context provided, this transform receives the output (which can be a string or object) along with a context that includes `vars`, `prompt`, and optional provider `metadata`. The transform processes this output and returns the value to pass to the assertions. If `null` or `undefined` is returned, an error occurs.\n\nFor example, in the context of JSON-formatted outputs, the `transform` directive can be used to extract specific fields before running checks:\n\n```yaml\ntests:\n  - vars:\n      item: banana\n    options:\n      transform: JSON.parse(output).countries\n    assert:\n      - type: contains-any\n        value:\n          - Guatemala\n          - Costa Rica\n          - India\n          - Indonesia\n```\n\nThis example demonstrates how the `transform` directive preprocesses the output to extract the `countries` field for evaluation.",
